From e96a31b3bbfd9a6d649ae13f1026eb20f5b1c00b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Weppner <harry@weppner.dev>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:55:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test.sh: skip test-optimizer-callback.py

Its golden reference data (test/data/test-optimizer-callback-ref-*.npy)
was last updated in 69eb9d6e (2025-09-29), before 3270b6c5 "Reworked
regularization" (2026-06-20) changed the optimizer output it compares.
It fails on upstream master regardless of the build environment.

Drop this patch once upstream refreshes the reference data.
---
 test.sh | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test.sh b/test.sh
index b58a1c99..eb1319b5 100755
--- a/test.sh
+++ b/test.sh
@@ -21,7 +21,6 @@ TESTS=("test/test-pywrap-functions.py"
        "test/test-gradients.py"
        "test/test-py-gradients.py"
        "test/test-cahvor"
-       "test/test-optimizer-callback.py"
        "test/test-sfm-fixed-points.py"
        "test/test-sfm-regularization-unity-cam01.py"
        "test/test-sfm-triangulated-points.py"
